        "original_id": "ad306750-6bf7-5aec-b1fb-624684121bd6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: M. S. Swaminathan, Norman Borlaug, Gregory Conko\n- Topics: Green Revolution in India, high-yielding wheat varieties, genetically modified food regulation\n- Works: The Frankenfood Myth\n- Awards: Nobel Peace Prize, Presidential Medal of Freedom, Congressional Gold Medal\n\nFacts:\n- In the Green Revolution in India, a main development was higher-yielding varieties of wheat.\n- Many scientists developed the higher-yielding wheat varieties, including Indian geneticist M. S. Swaminathan and American agronomist Norman Borlaug.\n- Norman Borlaug received multiple honors for his work, including the Nobel Peace Prize, the Presidential Medal of Freedom, and the Congressional Gold Medal.\n- The book The Frankenfood Myth argues against over-regulation of genetically modified food.\n- The Frankenfood Myth includes a foreword by Nobel Peace Prize-winner Norman Ernest Borlaug.",
